e that set them","p_rec":"If Baker City's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Baker City has set <strong>118 standing record lows</strong>, close to the 99 that chance alone would give, and <strong>131 record highs</strong>, more than the 99 that chance alone would give. The 2020s hold the most record highs of any decade (62). Baker City's all-time high is 109\u00b0F, on August 10, 2018.","t_chg":"Baker City's days got warmer. Its nights didn't.","p_chg":"Across 98 complete years: Baker City's average low shows no clear change: \u22120.13\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.25 to +0.00) that includes zero. It's close, but the range still includes zero. Baker City's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.26\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.14 to +0.37), about +2.5\u00b0F since 1928.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 1 of 12 months; 4 months fell. Highs rose in 7 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Baker City has gotten drier","p_rain":"Baker City's yearly precipitation has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.17 inches per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.34 to \u22120.00), about \u22121.6 inches since 1928. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 9.0 inches a year. The wettest year was 1978 (15.76 in); the driest, 2020 (3.36 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 8 daily record highs, 3 daily record lows"}}